{"title":"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9673ee04316e55d232ae3a9b8ce356386c0dc66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is written as a product of two positive integers whose difference is as small as possible, then the difference is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eaf08ec951184e9886119e6c5e1a2eb3be4041a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }8 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }15 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }17 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }47 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we want the difference of the two factors to be as small as possible, then the two numbers must be as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/80511ca5dc50b0bef29bd38f754bdeff95172866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1998}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> as possible.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/779f216c74ee287256d39b586d92171189ae882e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^2 = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, the factors should be as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as possible.\n</p><p>Breaking down <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9673ee04316e55d232ae3a9b8ce356386c0dc66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> into its prime factors gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3092e4e9f37b7f8bd6d450fc0b4372191a34f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1998 = 2\\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> is relatively close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and no numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9673ee04316e55d232ae3a9b8ce356386c0dc66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1998$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus, the two factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b5827a628e4057f5a46e29370bf884b444115b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^3 = 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />, and the difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fcb124818045c349a0e571d68b3969a15d3fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$54 - 37 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME\" title=\"1998 AHSME\">1998 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7